{"id": "4f60f619-9cbe-41dd-878a-72e4737a1c96", "timestamp": "2026-10-23T04:17:34.867444", "source": "user", "parent_id": "dec5dc6e-a163-463a-b96a-80b2cece1ed5", "llm_message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"cache_prompt": false, "type": "text", "text": "{\"researcher_request\": \"Чёрт, окей, let's scope this before we go anywhere. This is initial_inspection only — do NOT draft the full design yet. I need three things back from you, in this order, and nothing more right now. Keep it tight, no fluff, I'll ask follow-ups after I read what you actually find vs. what you assume. My brain doesn't do well with made-up certainty, so flag every guess clearly as a guess — I'd rather see five labeled assumptions than one confident paragraph that turns out to be fiction. Готов? Погнали. 1) Repository inspection. What's actually in /workspace? Run `ls -la /workspace` and show me the tree (depth 2 is fine). Read track.md in full and quote or summarize it. Then check whether any game code, agent scaffolding, RL framework, simulator wrapper, or config files already exist on disk — I want to know whether I'm designing on a blank sheet or inheriting something. Don't guess about files you haven't opened. Note that the environment has no network, no GPU, 24 CPU, and Python 3 only — so any design that needs PyTorch with CUDA download or live game telemetry is dead on arrival; flag if you see anything that requires more than that and don't claim network access you don't have. 2) Concretize the question. The brief is abstract; show me your read of it, in one short paragraph, then a bulleted list of what needs to be pinned down before any design is sensible — at minimum: what game / simulator is implied by 'pirate invasions when score threshold is reached' (is there one in this repo? if not, name the most defensible open candidate and say why), what exactly counts as 'built-in game mechanics' vs. agent-controlled behavior in this context (clarify the boundary — I'll reject any design that conflates them), and what 'hierarchical' vs 'non-hierarchical' means operationally (command structure? policy hierarchy? role assignment? module decomposition? each implies a different experiment — pick one and justify, don't blend). Don't paper over ambiguity to look decisive; I'd rather see 'I don't know yet — options A or B' than a premature commitment. 3) Proposed approach sketch. Don't write the experiment, write the *shape*: a 2x2 (or however you justify) factor structure in one line, the primary dependent variable with units, the planned control conditions, the rough measurement window or stopping rule, and how you'd randomize / replicate given 24 cores and a no-network sandbox. Then list the consequential assumptions and uncertainties you'd carry into design — including what you do NOT know about the game, the agent implementations, the score-threshold trigger logic, and the runtime budget. Label each item [ASSUMPTION] or [UNKNOWN] so I can hunt them. Stop there — do not produce the final design, do not produce analysis code, do not fabricate results. Submit just these three sections and wait for my next message.\", \"required_handoff_stage\": \"plan\", \"approach_approved\": false, \"public_task\": {\"question\": \"Does the triggering of built-in game mechanics, such as pirate invasions when the score threshold is reached, affect the survival durations of hierarchical versus non-hierarchical agents?\", \"context\": \"Design an experiment that answers the question. The researcher can clarify source-supported setup details by topic. Do not claim that an experiment was run.\", \"environment\": {\"runtime\": \"bubblewrap\", \"network\": \"disabled\", \"repository\": \"/workspace\", \"python\": \"python3\", \"software_environment\": \"system Python; project dependencies not preinstalled\", \"datasets\": [], \"gpu_enabled\": false, \"cpu_affinity_count\": 24, \"note\": \"Successful exploratory commands are not proof of a completed experiment.\"}, \"researcher_topics\": [], \"question_budget\": 6, \"actor_step_budget\": 60, \"continue_after_initial_plan\": false}}"}], "tool_calls": null, "tool_call_id": null, "name": null}, "llm_response_id": null, "activated_skills": [], "extended_content": [], "sender": null, "kind": "MessageEvent", "source_event_index": 1}
