t termination, cumulative damage received, number of pirate encounters survived.\n\n## Planned control conditions\n- **OFF cell:** same simulator, identical score-tracking code, **the score-threshold check evaluates but the spawn side-effect is suppressed**. Same RNG stream for score progression. Matched-everything-else control that isolates *the trigger's spawn behavior*, not the existence of score.\n- **Non-hierarchical baseline:** flat policy over the same atomic action set the hierarchical agent's sub-policies ultimately call. Where the hierarchical agent might terminate an option (\"flee ended at safe tile\"), the non-hierarchical agent must produce the same atomic sequence by direct action selection, but with no termination/meta gating.\n- **Pair-matched seeding:** each replicate in Hierarchical paired with a Non-hierarchical replicate initialized from the **same RNG seed** so observable rollout differences come from architecture, not stochasticity.\n\n## Measurement window / stopping rule\n- Per episode: hard cap (proposing 5,000 ticks; tune to ~10× expected median survival to avoid ceiling effects).\n- Across replicates: fixed **n = 30 per cell** (120 episodes total) as the minimum-feasible anchor. Revisit upward if pilot variance is large.\n- Aggregate stopping rule: per-cell collection terminates when 95% CI half-width on mean survival is < 10% of cross-cell pooled mean, or n hits cap.\n\n## Randomization & replication under 24 cores, no network\n- `multiprocessing.Pool(24)` — one run per worker task; results pickled back.\n- 120 episodes / 24 workers ≈ 5 waves. Workers stateless; each takes a `(seed, factor_A, factor_B)` tuple.\n- Seeds: master seed → Mersenne Twister-derived sub-seeds, recorded in a manifest so the run is reproducible from disk alone.\n- No I/O during episodes; only final per-episode summaries hit disk.\n\n## Consequential assumptions and unknowns to carry into design\n\n- **[ASSUMPTION]** No game exists in repo → the design specifies a 