4 justified by 24 schedulable cores, stdlib-only runtime, and the no-network/no-GPU constraint that rules out deep-RL training costs.\\n\", \"assumptions\": [\"No game exists in repo \\u2192 the design specifies a minimal, fully-described simulator with the score-threshold mechanic written down as a rule.\", \"Stdlib-only Python is sufficient (no torch / numpy / gym). Tabular or linear agents are the realistic substrate.\", \"Score-tracking is identical across ON and OFF cells; only the spawn side-effect of the threshold differs.\", \"Pair-matched seeds across Hierarchical / Non-hierarchical within a replicate so rollout differences are attributable to architecture, not RNG.\", \"\\\"Hierarchical\\\" = options/Feudal temporal hierarchy (meta-policy + sub-policies with termination), not module decomposition and not multi-agent command structure.\", \"Survival duration is measured in simulator ticks; mean and median both reported with 95% CIs.\", \"Agents are fixed policies for v1 (random / scripted); RL training is not in scope unless the researcher says otherwise.\", \"Single agent per episode; no peers, no multi-agent interactions.\", \"n=30 per cell is a defensible floor for v1, to be revisited upward if pilot variance is large.\", \"OFF control uses a matched-everything-else suppression of the spawn \\u2014 not removal of the score mechanic itself \\u2014 to keep game economy identical across cells.\"], \"uncertainties\": [\"Whether the researcher means real-RL, fixed-policy evaluation, or some scripted baseline by \\\"agent.\\\"\", \"Whether \\\"hierarchical\\\" means option-based HRL vs. module decomposition vs. multi-agent command structure.\", \"What terminates an episode \\u2014 pirate-induced death only, or do natural failures (resource, hazards) also end it.\", \"Whether the score threshold should be deterministic or stochastic, and where to set it relative to expected survival.\", \"Acceptable per-cell n, and whether the CI-half-width stopping rule is the right secondary criterion or should be replaced with a fixed n.\", \"Whether trajectory-level qualitative failure analyses are wanted as a design output, or strictly quantitative.\", \"Whether the comparison should also include a no-pirates-no-threshold condition (true baseline) on top of the score-threshold ON/OFF pair, or if matched OFF is sufficient.\"]}", "origin": "completion"}, "llm_response_id": "chatcmpl-133661ab-21c8-4bce-a8f8-719eff91018e", "security_risk": "UNKNOWN", "kind": "ActionEvent", "source_event_index": 18}
